#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124292 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "8ebce398-b228-51b0-8506-e0c6124478a5" :question/math-academy-id "e-6852" :question/problem "Find the differential for $f(x,y) = x^2 \\sin y$." :question/worked-solution "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= (\\frac{∂f}{∂x})dx + (\\frac{∂f}{∂y})dy \\\\\n&= (2x\\sin y)dx + (x^{2}\\cos y)dy \\\\\n&= 2x\\sin ydx + x^{2}\\cos ydy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124293 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/id #uuid "bb3ab0dc-7e26-58f5-a0c2-564c01c77f2e" :question/math-academy-id "e-6854" :question/problem "Given a cone, find the differential $\\textrm d V$ for the volume $V$ of the cone if the radius is $r=6$ and the height is $h = 3$." :question/worked-solution "The volume of the cone is\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\pi r^2h\n$$\n\nLet's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndV(r, h) &= (\\frac{∂V}{∂r})dr + (\\frac{∂V}{∂h})dh \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}πrhdr + \\frac{1}{3}πr^{2}dh\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6$ and $h=3$, the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndV(6, 3) &= \\frac{2}{3}π \\cdot 6 \\cdot 3dr + \\frac{1}{3}π \\cdot 6^{2}dh \\\\\n&= 12πdr + 12πdh\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124294 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab023be2-0156-5de6-8843-5b720775d649" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Change in a Multivariable Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0c4816ed-fba0-5dc7-94ba-646b875d653d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6875" :question/problem "If $f (x, y) = xe^y$, use the differential $\\textrm d f$ to estimate the change $\\Delta f$ in the value of $f(x, y)$ from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1)$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= (\\frac{∂f}{∂x})dx + (\\frac{∂f}{∂y})dy \\\\\n&= e^{y}dx + xe^{y}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(5,0)$, the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(5, 0) &= e^{0}dx + 5e^{0}dy \\\\\n&= 1dx + 5dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(5 + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y)$, then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx 1 \\, \\Delta x + 5 \\, \\Delta y\n$$\n\nMoving from $(5,0)$ to $(2,1)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔx &= 2 - 5 =-3, \\\\\nΔy &= 1 - 0 = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nΔf \\mid \\approx 1Δx + 5Δy; \\approx 1 \\cdot (-3) + 5 \\cdot (1); \\approx 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124295 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "febc72d4-b1b8-52c9-a805-013b30695077" :question/math-academy-id "e-6876" :question/problem "Estimate $\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)$ using a differential of the function $f(x,y) = \\sin x + \\cos y$ at the point $\\left(\\pi, 0 \\right)$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= (\\frac{∂f}{∂x})dx + (\\frac{∂f}{∂y})dy \\\\\n&= \\cos xdx - \\sin ydy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point\n\n$$\n\\left(\\pi, 0 \\right)\n$$\n\nthe differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndf(x, y) &= \\cos πdx - \\sin 0dy \\\\\n&=-1dx + 0dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\pi + \\Delta x, 0 + \\Delta y)$, then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\n\\Delta f \\approx -1 \\, \\Delta x + 0 \\, \\Delta y\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)= f(3,0.2)\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3,0.2)$.\n\nMoving from $(\\pi, 0)$ to $(3,0.2)$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nΔx &= 3 - π \\approx - 0.141, \\\\\nΔy &= 0.2 - 0 = 0.2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nΔf \\mid \\approx - 1(-0.141) + 0(0.2); \\approx 0.141\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.141$. Consequently, we have\n\n$$\nf(3, 0.2)\\begin{vmatrix}\\approx f(π, 0) + 0.141 \\\\ \\sin (3) + \\cos (0.2)\\end{vmatrix}\\approx \\sin (π) + \\cos (0) + 0.141; \\approx 0 + 1 + 0.141; \\approx 1.141\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "acafc931-a294-5ca7-8e39-cf8be29f08a9" :knowledge-point/title "Using Differentials to Approximate the Value of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0179cc13-dd1b-5d3b-9518-143e2445e69a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.417" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122825} {:answer/id #uuid "35d534f9-0842-5c39-b538-5a116c35e692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.556" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122826} {:answer/id #uuid "50ae4762-cb31-5fe1-b0bf-2a2dadbc049b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.873" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122827} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5b9594-1bd0-5656-9186-2c9c0bd4c3d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.215" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122828} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff33b79-6cc3-577d-9c7d-6711a937ed8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.235" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0179cc13-dd1b-5d3b-9518-143e2445e69a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.417" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122825} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bf3930e-171a-5983-a3fc-5f746e20f57e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122824}] :question/id #uuid "c4f3d8c4-d372-512f-a12b-325fd0cb0744" :question/math-academy-id "q-37281" :question/problem "Estimate $\\sqrt[3]{10} + \\sqrt{150}$ using a differential $df$ of the function $f(x, y) = \\sqrt[3]{x} + \\sqrt{y}$ at the point $(8, 144)$. Round your answer to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8067b52c-da04-51be-83e7-1edb3b741faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}dr + \\frac{1}{8}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122837} {:answer/id #uuid "a3cfa7a3-067d-5243-9361-9adabafe2403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}dr + 8dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122838} {:answer/id #uuid "300d0677-dab4-5c46-b293-044cf57f1aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{4}dr + 4dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122839} {:answer/id #uuid "6bf20e9e-9e91-5e6b-a6ce-009dc2c92f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "πdr + 4dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122840} {:answer/id #uuid "6cdb5e3d-2da4-548e-92b9-49e537184e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{8}dr + \\frac{1}{8}dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3cfa7a3-067d-5243-9361-9adabafe2403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2}dr + 8dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122838} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3bb73f1-2c84-58a3-bb35-e53f79a07f60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122836}] :question/id #uuid "f9652424-c2ee-5706-a3c2-84b62902c6d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-37295" :question/problem "Given a sector of a circle, find the differential $dS$ for the surface area $S$ if the radius is $r = 4$ and the central angle is $θ = \\frac{π}{8}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f23c5c7-d281-54da-b625-412925c80667" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Differential of a Multivariable Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ff4e387-63e7-5f7b-87b1-c005d396c662" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xdx}{x + y^{2}} + \\frac{2ydy}{x + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122855} {:answer/id #uuid "c301c3e7-1645-5ecf-8752-8fafbfe877f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dx}{x + y^{2}} + \\frac{2ydy}{x + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122856} {:answer/id #uuid "c9528693-d3a6-537a-9a1a-8be6ce9e29aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2dx}{x + y^{2}} - \\frac{2dy}{x + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122857} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ebb781-d343-5f08-9b34-71ead3dc5b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + y^{2})dx + (x + y^{2})dy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122858} {:answer/id #uuid "0c08229d-6c25-55f1-ae56-5b1e62eeac54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dx}{x + y^{2}} + \\frac{ydy}{x + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c301c3e7-1645-5ecf-8752-8fafbfe877f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dx}{x + y^{2}} + \\frac{2ydy}{x + y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122856} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e7d02a2-0bf4-5dec-b00c-6b2655731205" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122854}] :question/id #uuid "3d0cda7b-1864-5320-acd1-fb1c921ad388" :question/math-academy-id "q-37307" :question/problem "Find the differential $df$ for the function $f(x, y) = \\ln (x + y^{2})$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "153739f2-df62-5baf-8438-225edfc33ecb" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Differential in a Geometrical Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/